Database schema changes use Flask-Migrate/Alembic.

For a new database, apply the complete schema with:

    flask --app flask_app db upgrade

For a database created by the previous application version, mark its current
schema as the baseline, then apply the authorization-code migration:

    flask --app flask_app db stamp 0001_existing_schema
    flask --app flask_app db upgrade

When models change, generate a migration, review the generated operations, and
apply it:

    flask --app flask_app db migrate -m "describe the schema change"
    flask --app flask_app db upgrade

Autogeneration compares model metadata with the database; it does not update
the schema when the application starts.

Daily games require the daily-date migration. After upgrading, configure the
PythonAnywhere scheduled task to run `python /path/to/create_daily_game.py`
once at midnight in the `America/Los_Angeles` timezone. The script is safe to
retry for the same date; the database permits at most one daily game per date.
